sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User (browser)
    participant AC as AuthContext
    participant SB as Supabase Auth
    participant DB as Postgres (RLS)
    participant SB2 as Sidebar / ProtectedRoute

    Note over AC: App boot — listener registered before any fetch
    AC->>SB: onAuthStateChange(callback)
    AC->>SB: getSession()
    SB-->>AC: session | null

    alt session present
        AC->>DB: select * from profiles where user_id = auth.uid()
        DB-->>AC: profile (role, department, is_locked)
        AC->>DB: rpc get_user_roles(user_uuid)
        DB-->>AC: user_roles rows
        AC-->>AC: hydrate user { id, email, role, permissions }
    else no session
        AC-->>U: redirect to /login
    end

    U->>SB2: render app shell
    SB2->>AC: usePermissions() / user.role
    Note right of SB2: Sidebar filters nav items by permission;<br/>ProtectedRoute guards the route with the<br/>same permission key (navAccessConsistency test).

    alt permission granted
        SB2-->>U: render page
        U->>DB: page queries (select ...)
        DB-->>U: only rows the RLS policies allow
    else permission missing
        SB2-->>U: <AccessDenied /> (no data request issued)
    end

    Note over DB: RLS is the real boundary — a hand-crafted<br/>request from a hidden route still returns 0 rows.
